sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1022446A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO KK</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO &amp; CO. LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A superexpansive rotary engine having a rotor and a rotor housing, the rotor being rotated within the inner wall of the rotor housing. A gap between the rotor and the inner wall of the rotor housing defines an engine chamber. A plurality of extensible sealing blades in the rotor are mounted in substantially equally spaced positions on the circle of the rotor to elastically slide along the inner wall of the rotor housing to air-tightly separate the rotor engine chamber. As a result, the engine wherein suction, compression and exhaust of combustion gases are effected has a compression chamber and an expansion chamber, each being defined by two adjacent sealing blades, and the expansion chamber is larger than the compression chamber in maximum capacity.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un moteur rotatif à superexpansion, possédant un rotor et un logement de rotor, le rotor étant mis en rotation dans l'espace délimité par la paroi interne du logement du rotor. Un espace entre le rotor et la paroi intérieure dudit logement de rotor définit une chambre de moteur. Plusieurs ailettes d'étanchéité de rotor extensibles sont montées selon un espacement sensiblement régulier, sur le moyeu du rotor, de sorte qu'elles glissent élastiquement le long de la paroi intérieure du logement du rotor et qu'elles séparent de manière hermétique la chambre du moteur à rotor. Ainsi, le moteur dans lequel l'aspiration, la compression et l'échappement des gaz s'effectuent, comporte une chambre de compression, une chambre d'expansion, définies chacune par deux ailettes d'étanchéité adjacentes, la chambre d'expansion présentant une capacité maximum supérieure à celle de la chambre de compression.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>